  "hypothesis": "H73-1: Unmapped geothermal-indicative faults in NW Nevada / Walker Lane are best recovered by uniting (1) closed-form Quaternary piedmont geomorphology (cross-drainage bajada contour orthogonality |sin(theta_scarp - theta_fan)|, relief-normalized scarp prominence step/(relief+12m), 1.6 km along-strike true-elevation variance separating fan-climbing tectonic scarps from horizontal Pleistocene Lake Lahontan wave-cut shorelines, and 12-azimuth 2.1 km steerable Radon anisotropy) in a 91-feature 100% zero-SGMC multi-tree ensemble with (2) a 24-channel 2D Multi-Scale Dilated Residual U-Net trained end-to-end with Exact 300 m Differentiable Kernel DTI Loss, emitted via concave probability calibration, DrivenData Staff 11516/4 tip-protected flank gating, and exact 300 m submodular DTI max-cover.",
